    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a108cf3c9bcae9250d85b09d65216e4c9a4c1d5edc8ba9b166d020689dfa8c74",
      "text": "After breakfast, continue fishing in the Flamingo area.\n\nThe main fishing grounds are out in the open ocean, where the water quickly deepens and large pelagic species are found, and closer to the Catalina and Brummel islands.\n\nIn deep water, you may catch sailfish, several species of marlin, dorado, yellowfin tuna and bigeye tuna. Around the islands, look for wahoo, Sierra mackerel, Spanish mackerel, bigeye trevally, Pacific sea bass and roosterfish.\n\nOvernight at **Tamarindo Diria**.\n\nMeals: breakfast and lunch.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-98c5fe36c1a7",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
    },
